r (`DumpJavaStack`) and logs:\n    `LOG(WARNING) << \"Monitor contention with tid \" << owner_tid << \", wait time: \" << wait_ms << \"ms, monitor id: \" << monitor_id_ << \"\\nPerfMonitor owner thread(\" << owner_tid << \") stack is:\\n\" << owner_stack_dump`.\n  * *(Implementation quirk at `runtime/base/mutex.cc:489`)*: fallback when `Runtime::Current() == nullptr` assigns `Monitor::kDefaultMonitorTimeoutMs` (`500` ns instead of `MsToNs(500)`) to `timeout_ts.tv_nsec`, though `Runtime::Current()` is always non-null for active Java monitors.\n\n### 3.4 Thread Priority & Priority Inversion Mitigation\n* **`ScopedPriorityChange`** (`runtime/scoped_thread_priority_change.h:45-78`, `runtime/scoped_thread_priority_change.cc:27-79`):\n  * Gated by trunk-stable flag `com::android::libcore::niceness_apis()`.\n  * `SetToNormalOrBetter()` checks `self_->GetCachedNiceness() > 0` (background/low priority) and `getpriority(PRIO_PROCESS, 0) == cached_niceness`, then calls `setpriority(PRIO_PROCESS, 0, 0)` (boosting niceness to `0`) until `ResetInternal()` restores `cached_niceness`.\n  * **Callsites preventing GC/alloc priority inversion**:\n    1. `Heap::AllocateInternalWithGc` (`runtime/gc/heap.cc:2039-2040`): boosts background threads performing blocking GC-for-alloc.\n    2. `MarkCompact::RunPhases` (`runtime/gc/collector/mark_compact.cc:878, 885, 892, 898, 910`): boosts GC thread while weak-reference access is disabled (from end of `MarkingPhase` until `ReclaimPhase` re-enables weak refs) and across compaction thread-flip.\n    3. `ConcurrentCopying::RunPhases` & `MarkingPhase` (`runtime/gc/collector/concurrent_copying.cc:230, 1630`): boosts GC thread during critical root-flip and reference-processing windows.\n* **Design Constraints (`runtime/thread_priorities.md:1-221`)**:\n  * Documents Android's 3 priority layers (Java `1..10`, Linux niceness `-20..19` mapped via `PaletteMapPriority`, and `SCHED_FIFO` RT `1..99`), warns that `SCHED_FIFO` threads break ART thin-lock spin/yield loops if holding locks contended by higher-RT threads (`L129-145`), and explains why `FUTEX_LOCK_PI` priority inheritance is not yet enabled on ART monitors/mutexes (`SCHED_OTHER` PI requires Linux `>= 6.12` and incompatible futex word layouts, `L192-221`).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Vendor / OEM Custom Modifications Check\n\n* **Result: Clean Upstream AOSP (Android 15 / V) — No Proprietary OEM / QTI Customizations Found.**\n  * Every inspected file in `art/runtime/`, `art/perfetto_hprof/`, and `art/libartbase/` matches upstream AOSP Android 15:\n    * Zero Voyah, Dongfeng, or Qualcomm (`libqti-perfd`, `perf_hint`, vendor hooks) modifications exist in `art/runtime/gc/`, `art/runtime/monitor*`, `art/runtime/base/`, `art/perfetto_hprof/`, `art/runtime/javaheapprof/`, or `art/runtime/hprof/`.\n    * `/home/ethen/workspace/voyah/projects/8397/code/qssi/system/libartpalette/palette_android_partner.cc:66-73` is also the unmodified AOSP stub (`PaletteReportLockContention` returns `PALETTE_STATUS_OK` without custom vendor telemetry forwarding).\n    * The `MonitorTimeoutEnable` / `\"PerfMonitor owner thread\"` feature in `monitor.cc` and `base/mutex.cc` (originally contributed by OEM engineers) is part of upstream AOSP `platform/art` and is disabled by default (`MonitorTimeoutEnable = false`, not enabled in `AndroidRuntime.cpp`).\n    * `git status` in `art/` shows only one untracked test file (`artd/tests/src/UpdateApplication.java`).\n</SYSTEM_MESSAGE>"}
